No third-party source is included here. The build and the evaluation use the material below,
each fetched from its own project and staying under its own licence.

1. NVIDIA RAPIDS Accelerator for Apache Spark (cudf-spark), under the Apache License, Version 2.0

   The plugin is compiled against the released rapids-4-spark jar, and
   scripts/build-rapids-patch.sh replaces classes in a copy of that jar with ones built from
   https://github.com/beestream-ai/cudf-spark, branch feature/tornadovm-udf-fallback, a fork of
   https://github.com/NVIDIA/cudf-spark. Those changes stay under the RAPIDS project's Apache 2.0
   licence and keep its file headers. Nothing here relicenses them, and no file here ships in
   NVIDIA's package namespace.

2. NVIDIA spark-rapids-examples, under the Apache License, Version 2.0

   The MovieLens application's 'native' mode loads NVIDIA's published native cosine-similarity
   UDF, from https://github.com/NVIDIA/spark-rapids-examples, reflectively when it is on the class
   path, as the B3 baseline. Nothing of NVIDIA's is compiled or redistributed here; the harness
   that builds it is in https://github.com/beestream-ai/spark-jitudf-benchmarking.

3. TornadoVM, under the Apache License, Version 2.0

   https://github.com/beehive-lab/TornadoVM, used as a released SDK and as the Maven artifacts
   io.github.beehive-lab:tornado-api and io.github.beehive-lab:tornado-runtime.

4. Apache Spark, under the Apache License, Version 2.0

   https://spark.apache.org, used as the stock binary distribution, unmodified.

5. The MovieLens 25M data set, under the GroupLens research licence

   The evaluation prepares its inputs from MovieLens 25M (F. M. Harper and J. A. Konstan,
   "The MovieLens Datasets: History and Context", ACM TiiS 5(4), 2015,
   https://doi.org/10.1145/2827872), downloaded by the reader from
   https://files.grouplens.org/datasets/movielens/ml-25m.zip under the terms stated there.
   No MovieLens data is redistributed in this repository.
